{"schemaVersion":1,"corpusId":"euclid-elements-heath-1908","status":"raw_machine","contentItem":{"id":"euclid-3-5","kind":"proposition","title":"两圆相交必不同心","englishTitle":"If two circles cut one another, they will not have the same centre.","book":3,"number":5,"status":"raw_machine","sourceMissing":false,"source":{"urn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.5","url":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.5/","group":"prop","sourceNumber":5,"corpusSha256":"ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c","hasSourceFigure":true,"historicalChineseUrl":"https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/幾何原本/卷三"}},"revision":{"id":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","contentId":"euclid-3-5","version":1,"status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"5d18af9687814ff59a6149e194b47a04eb5c8499631fd13a0887dd4e06b6147e","createdBy":"mathforge-corpus-import","changeSummary":"Imported Heath source and machine-assisted Chinese draft. No mathematical or editorial review is implied.","blockIds":["euclid-3-5.statement","euclid-3-5.construction.1","euclid-3-5.proof.1","euclid-3-5.proof.2","euclid-3-5.proof.3","euclid-3-5.proof.4","euclid-3-5.proof.5","euclid-3-5.conclusion","euclid-3-5.historical.1","euclid-3-5.source"]},"blocks":[{"id":"euclid-3-5.statement","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":0,"kind":"statement","title":"命题陈述","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"8cc7a84359fb490a1343b8fb0e0550a04f36739f5ab0df1edd246f24174eff1b","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"If two circles cut one another, they will not have the same centre."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果两个圆圈互相切开,它们就不会有相同的中心。"},{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"两圜相交必不同心"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"当两个圆相交时，它们的圆心必须不同"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.construction.1","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":1,"kind":"construction","title":"作图与构造 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"219bc6b00d06ddc7d407a12f723967e39ebb617920a6badb10b5dbbf7b244830","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For let the circles ABC, CDG cut one another at the points B, C; I say that they will not have the same centre."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"让ABC,CDG圈在B,C点相互切开;我说,它们将没有相同的中心。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.proof.1","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":2,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"249234476e9a92bef015b30ccfdf87bc817151f26a19c3609d9b8eb382e59d6d","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"For, if possible, let it be E; let EC be joined, and let EFG be drawn through at random."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"如果可能的话,让它为E;让EC连接,让EFG随机通过。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.proof.2","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":3,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 2","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"314055b92ab98e66b9c91e21022f7906e2198c2d44e40d69d8f7fc377888b56e","citations":["euclid-1-def-15"],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Then, since the point E is the centre of the circle ABC, EC is equal to EF. [[I. Def. 15](/principles/euclid-1-def-15)]"},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"礛由于E点是ABC点的中心,EC等于EF点。 [[I. Def. 15](/principles/euclid-1-def-15)]"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.proof.3","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":4,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 3","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"94fc4a90838f92d4a9c02ce9a4c492ff9bde9c90b1fdd7de821e8c90307886eb","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Again, since the point E is the centre of the circle CDG, EC is equal to EG."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"同样,由于E点是CDG点的中心,EC点等于EG点。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.proof.4","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":5,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 4","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"df3fd2a8ea1daafac3e4da680b6f2fc95f86dafeb2dc2ae57b7356ae779f7213","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"But EC was proved equal to EF also; therefore EF is also equal to EG, the less to the greater : which is impossible."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"EC 也等于EF,EF 也等于EG, 数量小于数量大为不可能。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.proof.5","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":6,"kind":"proof_step","title":"证明 5","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"f590c9b631e8a589d6b2e7143cd9a0c5acfb95748dbaf7476b6e25cecfeb61eb","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore the point E is not the centre of the circles ABC, CDG."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,E点不是圆圈的中心,ABC,CDG。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.conclusion","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":7,"kind":"conclusion","title":"结论","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"d41f4fe56dd428c759377c807a93013dffbbe29c7596acfdac57dd182cad51b6","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"heath-en","role":"source","language":"en","status":"source_transcription","text":"Therefore etc. Q. E. D."},{"id":"machine-zh","role":"machine_translation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"因此,等等,证毕。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.historical.1","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":8,"kind":"historical_note","title":"徐光启、利玛窦历史中译 1","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"134622baceb63c6f7aeb96a88a4a4cc7f65981829de2df84f56a7d931990c065","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"historical-zh","role":"historical_source","language":"zh-Hans","status":"source_transcription","text":"两圜相交必不同心解曰甲乙丁戊乙丁两圜交于乙于丁题言两圜不同心论曰若言丙为同心令自丙至乙至甲各作直线其丙乙至圜交而丙甲截两圜之界于戊于甲夫丙既为戊乙丁圜之心则丙乙与丙戊等而又为甲乙丁圜之心则丙乙与丙甲又等是丙戊与丙甲亦等而全与其分等也"},{"id":"historical-modern-zh","role":"historical_machine_interpretation","language":"zh-CN","status":"raw_machine","text":"两个圆相交时，圆心必须不同心。解释如下：甲乙丁戊乙丁，两个圆在乙与丁相交。命题解释：两个圆不共心的证明如下：如果丙是同心圆，并从丙到乙到甲画一条直线，则丙乙与圆相交，丙甲在两个圆的边界处于戊与甲相交。如果丙是戊乙丁的中心，则丙乙和丙戊是中心，甲乙丁是圆的中心。则丙乙和丙甲也相等，所以丙戊和丙甲也相等，且所有部分都相等。"}]},{"id":"euclid-3-5.source","contentId":"euclid-3-5","revisionId":"euclid-3-5@raw-5d18af9687814ff5","order":9,"kind":"source","title":"来源、译者与开放许可","status":"raw_machine","contentHash":"695eadc8a9e764fbc8c40016758f8c281ec94abda150d333988af6d518bc4a1b","citations":[],"surfaces":[{"id":"provenance","role":"provenance_note","language":"en","status":"generated_metadata","text":"Perseus / Heath source: https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.5/\nCorpus URN: urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.5\nCorpus SHA-256: ba12e2e47aec41f853ff32929a2d0467926f93280f1bf8870bda5016c29d143c\nLicense: CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)\nHistorical Chinese source: https://zh.wikisource.org/zh-hans/幾何原本/卷三"}]}],"outgoingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-3-5:euclid-1-def-15:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-3-5","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-3-5.proof.2"],"targetContentId":"euclid-1-def-15","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.5","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.5/","sourceLabel":"I. Def. 15"}}],"incomingEdges":[{"id":"edge:euclid-3-10:euclid-3-5:explicit","sourceContentId":"euclid-3-10","sourceBlockIds":["euclid-3-10.proof.5"],"targetContentId":"euclid-3-5","type":"depends_on","provenance":{"kind":"explicit_source_reference","basis":"perseus_tei_ref","sourceUrn":"urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.10","sourceUrl":"https://scaife.perseus.org/reader/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg1799.tlg001.perseus-eng2:3.prop.10/","sourceLabel":"III. 5"}}],"dependencies":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-3-5:euclid-1-def-15:explicit","id":"euclid-1-def-15","book":1,"number":15,"kind":"definition","title":"圆：到圆心距离相等的点形成的图形","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"dependents":[{"edgeId":"edge:euclid-3-10:euclid-3-5:explicit","id":"euclid-3-10","book":3,"number":10,"kind":"proposition","title":"两个圆至多相交于两点","provenance":"explicit_source_reference"}],"visualization":{"level":"concept_illustration","rendererId":"concept-circle","rationale":"The current renderer is selected by a broad geometry family and must not be presented as this proposition’s exact construction."},"sourceIssues":[]}
